Data sources
------------

Aloft bird migration data repository (https://aloftdata.eu)
  Vertical profiles of birds derived from European weather radars.
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Attribution: "Contains data from the Aloft bird migration data repository
  (aloftdata.eu), CC BY 4.0."

EUMETNET OPERA Open Radar Data
  Single-site polar volumes and composites from European national weather
  services, published as high-value datasets.
  Licence: CC BY 4.0, with exceptions noted in the metadata of individual
  radars; FlockLake checks the metadata of every radar it ingests.
  Attribution: "Contains data from EUMETNET OPERA Open Radar Data, CC BY 4.0."

NOAA NEXRAD Level II
  Polar volumes from the US WSR-88D network.
  Licence: open data from the US National Oceanic and Atmospheric
  Administration, without use restrictions.
  Attribution (requested): "NOAA National Weather Service Radar Operations
  Center, NEXRAD Level II, via NSF Unidata and the AWS Open Data Sponsorship
  Program."

Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com)
  Weather model and reanalysis data on pressure levels.
  Licence: CC BY 4.0.
  Attribution: "Weather data by Open-Meteo.com, CC BY 4.0."

Methods
-------

FlockLake's vertical-profile methods follow published work, implemented
independently in Python. See docs/research/radar-aeroecology.md and
CITATION.cff, in particular:

  Dokter, A. M., et al. (2011). Bird migration flight altitudes studied by a
  network of operational weather radars. Journal of the Royal Society
  Interface 8(54), 30-43. doi:10.1098/rsif.2010.0116

  Dokter, A. M., et al. (2019). bioRad: biological analysis and visualization
  of weather radar data. Ecography 42(5), 852-860. doi:10.1111/ecog.04028

vol2bird (https://github.com/adokter/vol2bird, MIT licence) is used only as an
external reference implementation in tests and is not distributed with
FlockLake.
